<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-suzukii-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila suzukii Turing onset wavelength at 2.046 µm (0 Ma, detail scale) (Drosophila suzukii)",
        "Drosophila suzukii Turing onset wavelength at 2.046 µm (0 Ma, detail scale) faithfully reproduces Drosophila suzukii morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-suzukii-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-suzukii-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-suzukii-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-suzukii-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila suzukii specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-suzukii-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila suzukii" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That D. takahashii's pigment wavelength has been measured at 2.455 µm.",
        "does_not_claim: That subobscura → suzukii → takahashii is a fossil ancestor chain. All three are Holocene (0 Ma); the order is the comparative chronoseries.",
        "does_not_claim: That yellow or ebony kinetics are Schnakenberg reactions, or that D_u and D_v were measured.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg a=0.037, b=1.284, D_v/D_u=12.6, D_u solved so the onset wavelength is 2.046 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Subobscura uses a=0.52, b=0.18 so f_u = -17/35 and the Turing band is absent.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Takahashii keeps the kinetics and multiplies both diffusivities by 1.44, so lambda_c = 2.4552 µm (10 waves in the same window instead of 12).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: The periodic window quantizes a stripe seed onto lambda_c = 2.046 µm even though the fastest linear wavelength is 2.116 µm.",
        "reported_in_source: A two-species reaction-diffusion system selects a finite onset wavenumber k_c (Turing 1952).",
        "reported_in_source: Male D. suzukii has an apical wing spot; the female has a serrated ovipositor (Atallah 2014).",
        "reported_in_source: Spot presence in the suzukii–biarmipes clade is a yellow cis-regulatory gain (Gompel 2005; Prud'homme 2006; Koshikawa 2020).",
        "transfer_boundary: 2.046 µm is the campaign detail-scale assignment, not a measured granule spacing.",
        "transfer_boundary: The McEvey plate (960×640, 1 mm bar) anchors the animal. It does not resolve the carrier." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila suzukii (Spotted-Wing Drosophila)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-suzukii-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_suzukii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila suzukii; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Male D. suzukii has an apical wing spot; the female has a serrated ovipositor (Atallah 2014). | Spot presence in the suzukii–biarmipes clade is a yellow cis-regulatory gain (Gompel 2005; Prud'homme 2006; Koshikawa 2020). | A two-species reaction-diffusion system selects a finite onset wavenumber k_c (Turing 1952).; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg a=0.037, b=1.284, D_v/D_u=12.6, D_u solved so the onset wavelength is 2.046 µm. | Subobscura uses a=0.52, b=0.18 so f_u = -17/35 and the Turing band is absent. | Takahashii keeps the kinetics and multiplies both diffusivities by 1.44, so lambda_c = 2.4552 µm (10 waves in the same window instead of 12). | The periodic window quantizes a stripe seed onto lambda_c = 2.046 µm even though the fastest linear wavelength is 2.116 µm.; transfer_boundary: 2.046 µm is the campaign detail-scale assignment, not a measured granule spacing. | The McEvey plate (960×640, 1 mm bar) anchors the animal. It does not resolve the carrier.; does_not_claim: That yellow or ebony kinetics are Schnakenberg reactions, or that D_u and D_v were measured. | That D. takahashii's pigment wavelength has been measured at 2.455 µm. | That subobscura → suzukii → takahashii is a fossil ancestor chain. All three are Holocene (0 Ma); the order is the comparative chronoseries.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
